WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.762
Because the easy fix is the wrong one.

3
00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:07.166
An administrator who grants
the itil role to make

4
00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:10.651
it work has given the
integration every ITSM table.

5
00:00:10.651 --> 00:00:15.338
An API client with a manage scope can
change accounts if its token is stolen.

6
00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:18.092
One integration user
for everything means the

7
00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:21.200
account that reads evidence
can also close findings.

8
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.827
And when a client gains
a call nobody listed,

9
00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:27.475
someone grants a role in production
to make the error go away.

10
00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:31.900
Each of those has a guard in the kit, and
you'll use every one of them in the lab.

11
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.415
The idea of the module is simple: confirm
the boundary on paper first, then make

12
00:00:36.415 --> 00:00:41.060
privilege something a test can check,
instead of something someone remembers.
